{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player","id":956214,"title":"Looking for advice on how to deal with a player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-23T01:59:40-07:00","id":956214,"title":"Looking for advice on how to deal with a player","content":"I am currently running a Second edition Requiem game set in Los Angeles, and so far things have been going very smoothly except for one player. He plays a Nosferatu Gardener Bloodline that has that double bite which does additional lethal and I can't calm him down. I had the local elder warn him to stop leaving a trail of bodies, but he keeps killing anything in his path, he also has instakilled the vamp I sent to deal with him doing about 5-7 lethal per bite. I've kindly tried to stop the player, but he's forcing me to kill character as if I am to remove him other players would follow.<br /> <br /> He has Obsfucate 3, 4 dots into Riding the Wave, a full grappling style, and 5 Strength.<br /> <br /> All i'm asking is how do I deal with this character, how would I catch him by surprise or kill him swiftly so he doesn't try to run off. In my game I have npc supernaturals in the form of Werewolves, Hunters, Mages, and Strix. Any feedback or suggestions in how to stop the nonstop killing would be greatly appreciated thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:16:14-07:00","id":956235,"title":"","content":"If talking to the player doesn't work, then you probably need a new player. Even if you kill this character, the next willbprobably cause just as many problems.<br /> <br /> Strix can take him down by default. Or they could just possess him.<br /> <br /> This dude's humanity should be dropping like crazy. Draugr is an appropriate end to such a character.<br /> <br /> Vigor staking or vigor grapple + bite help. Throw in a dot of celerity to cheat initiative so he cant get obfuscate off. Having vigor + brawl means they can handle themselves in a grapple.<br /> <br /> Protean 3, Swarm Form is a thing he cant bite his way out of. Same with Protean 5.<br /> <br /> A Rahu or Irraka can probably go toe to toe in a grapple.<br /> <br /> A group of hunters, some of whom have clear sighted could take him out. Traps. Flamethrowers. Etc. This may be the best option since you can tue their going after hin with the trail of dead bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:04:17-07:00","id":956250,"title":"","content":"A vampire with Vigor + brawl and obfuscate 3 could end the fight in the first turn. Grapple him with a surprise attack using vitae to rise strenght, with 5 successes (you don't must to subtract defence) he can bite in the same turn with, at least, 5 lethal damage, adding Vigor (depending on the BP expenditure but save a vitae point for Vigor).<br /> For example obfuscate 3, vigor 3, strenght 5, brawl 4, BP 3 npc could works.<br /> She grapples with 16 dice (2 vitae to rise 4 at strenght) that can easily result in 5 successes. So 5 lethal damages with bite and +3 vigor. I think 8 damages is enought to send him in torpor. I doubt he could have more than 3 in stamina. Otherwise just rise the stats to your will. It's not weird that a vampire who kills another vampire and go around killing everyone could be hunted by a bad ass like a sheriff maybe.<br /> <br /> Or simply let him meet a dominate/Majesty master: \u300atake the car go &quot;some place isolated like a desert&quot; and walk trhough &quot;a direction where there is nothing&quot;.\u300b<br /> He will walk till the sun rise and when he wake up he will not have a place where to hide from the sun.<br /> Or even:\u300a let me drink from you\u300b with Majesty or domination. Drinking from a vampire does not deal damage so he would not wake up. Drain him so he could not have blood to use obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-23-2016, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:19:59-07:00","id":956254,"title":"","content":"Really, if talking with the player does not help you will need a new player. Even if you kill his current character, his next one will most likely be as bad (otherwise, simply talking with him would do the trick). Killing him is easy, Celerity will wreck him completely (due to lost initiative) and a killing method of your choice. What you should really be worried about in this case, is how you set the expectations for his next character, as you shouldn't let in such combos in again. <br /> <br /> And also be ready to have a bitter player on your hands, as he will feel/know that the events were arranged specifically to kill off his character. <br /> <br /> TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R; talk with the player. If he doesn't see a problem find a new player","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:24:52-07:00","id":956256,"title":"","content":"I'm of the idea that a character could do wathever he wants and learn in game why he couldn't.<br /> In this particular case kill or send in torpor his character could be a right thing. I mean: if in the real life I kill people, police will stops me. Same thing in vampire. So, next time, he will know that going on with this bheaviour will lead him to another brutal end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:02:22-07:00","id":956317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=956235#post956235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This dude's humanity should be dropping like crazy. Draugr is an appropriate end to such a character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily. The lower it is, the worst act it takes to lower it further.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm reminded of another game in which I had a similar player who was causing problems for everyone else (meta gaming, Mary Sue) and refused to change his ways. As the game master, I finally just took narrative control of the situation and killed the character off by having him torn in half by a giant monster. I banned them from any future games with me for several months after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:27:06-07:00","id":956333,"title":"","content":"I need more context. Are you unhappy with the player specifically or are you unhappy that their character is killing NPCs with impunity? What exactly do you think the player / character is doing wrong?<br /> <br /> edit: if it's just the character killing others with impunity, and you feel like there should be a consequence, then feel free to create scenarios where violence isn't the answer - put a pack of werewolves in his way; however, a pack of werewolves open to talking and sorting things out with words. If he doesn't use words, instead opting for fists, then he'll be in for a rude surprise as werewolves own the realm of fighting (should've used words).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 08-23-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:09:25-07:00","id":956357,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hear that you have that kind of player. As many others before me, i'm going to tell you that probably his next character will be a pain in the ass too.<br /> <br /> I would remind you, however, that you can <i>use him</i> as a story hook: maybe some ancient will regard him as a trained murderer, and will set in his way to &quot;acquire&quot; (blood bond, majesty, dominate, nightmare) him in order to use him as a thug or an assasin. That way you have him covered and &quot;happy&quot; in his particular(ly douche) playstyle, while you can send him ever greater threats (travel to the forest, i have this problem with a local werewolf. Oh, survived that? Well then, the werewolves mates will investigate that. The Elder is not happy having to deal with them, so he'll ask him again to clear the mess -and some minor, expendable npc to go with him-).<br /> <br /> Along the road, his humanity will erode at fast pace (and a draugr end to that player, with that very same ancient who employs him putting him down like a rabid dog, would be <i>most</i> fitting). <br /> <br /> Besides, if you follow this idea, such an Elder will have other powerful enemies, not to say the least another Elders. You can weave some different plots in that regard, maybe even kidnapping him and playing a &quot;flee the prison&quot; game(he inside, the others trying to free him). Maybe you can get some fun sessions out of that. <br /> <br /> In short, killing a character is super easy. Look no further than Cruac or Theban Sorcery, whose level 5 rituals can kill him from a basement, three cities away. Do you want a more personal approach? Any combination with Obfuscate + Offensive Discipline is devastating. Would you want some gore out of it? Pick Protean, Vigor and Resilience. Do you want to humiliate him? Majesty/Dominate + blood bond. Do you want to do it memorable? Play the vampire game: use human/ghoul pawns, and torch his place in broad daylight.<br /> <br /> [Or, again, the Draugr death. That's the worst (<b>best</b>) of them all, in my opinion.] <br /> <br /> But, if you can play <i>him</i>, bring him into the game offering some scenes tailor-made for his character, enjoying all the while some hard action game hours while you slowly draw the rope around his throat -so to speak- and let himself drag his humanity down while you teach the others something about the game philosophy... that is the road to awe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:13:18-07:00","id":956364,"title":"","content":"I am with the others. that if the player can not be talked to, then you need a new player. <br /> Also that if the character has been talked to about leaving bodies and that is a big no no. Send the sheriff after him. Majesty, Idol. They wont want to fight. Or a Dominate to have them spill all their vitae so they wont wake up. Or even Nightmare so they cant spend willpower against you. There are plenty of Non-physical ways to stop this character. <br /> <br /> I like the werewolf Idea. give him the chance to talk it out with wolves, if he picks a fight he will likely die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:24:23-07:00","id":956377,"title":"","content":"The question is whether this is an IC problem or an OOC one.<br /> <br /> Talk to the player. Always step one. Do they understand that their IC behavior is not ICly acceptable? Do they understand that their actions will have IC consequences, and are they willing to accept those consequences? That's good! It can provide story hooks. Provide IC consequences. Send the Sheriff and/or Hound after them. Throw in some other NPCs that have a vested interest. Other people have already provided good tips on the mechanical side.<br /> <br /> Do they not understand that it's not ICly acceptable? More specifically, are they not able or willing to handle the fact that IC actions = IC consequences? Are they ruining the fun for the other players? In such a case, there is no shame in telling them that this game isn't a good fit for them. Killing the PC won't solve your problem if the problem is the player, not the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:35:58-07:00","id":956381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player#post956214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently running a Second edition Requiem game set in Los Angeles, and so far things have been going very smoothly except for one player. He plays a Nosferatu Gardener Bloodline that has that double bite which does additional lethal and I can't calm him down. I had the local elder warn him to stop leaving a trail of bodies, but he keeps killing anything in his path, he also has instakilled the vamp I sent to deal with him doing about 5-7 lethal per bite. I've kindly tried to stop the player, but he's forcing me to kill character as if I am to remove him other players would follow.<br /> <br /> He has Obsfucate 3, 4 dots into Riding the Wave, a full grappling style, and 5 Strength.<br /> <br /> All i'm asking is how do I deal with this character, how would I catch him by surprise or kill him swiftly so he doesn't try to run off. In my game I have npc supernaturals in the form of Werewolves, Hunters, Mages, and Strix. Any feedback or suggestions in how to stop the nonstop killing would be greatly appreciated thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just curious, is it a problem for the vampires in the game but only? Or is it a problem for the story you trying to tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:01:16-07:00","id":956428,"title":"","content":"Sanctified Knight with enough Theban to combust his body to death should suffice. Alternatively? Anyone with a lit molotov cocktail inflicting the &quot;On Fire&quot; condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T00:09:39-07:00","id":956825,"title":"","content":"Thank you all, and to elaborate I have basically dropped to the player I want him to focus more on more of an aspect of just investigating the local happenings, but he is obbsessed with creating Lacmir that blood substitute from plants. he kills without discretion and gets away do to obsfucate, but I am liking the Theban sorcery idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T04:59:45-07:00","id":956887,"title":"","content":"What if any social merits does the group have? The way I see it he is making his clan look bad, risking the Maskarade and blowing off advice from an elder. The big question is how long before one of them makes a move and when the party hears about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:44:11-07:00","id":956992,"title":"","content":"First thing's first, sit down and have a talk with this player. Tell him, in no uncertain terms, that the way he's playing his character is not appropriate for the game you want to run. Explain clearly to him what the buy-in is for the story you are telling, and tell him he needs to make a character that will take part in the buy-in if he wants to play in this game. If he refuses, kick him out.<br /> <br /> Now, if that's not something you're willing to do, and you are only interested in in-character solutions, have word of the trouble his killing spree is causing reach the Prince. Have the Prince call a blood hunt on him, with Amaranth sanctioned for who ever brings him to justice. Let him decide if it's worth continuing to play a character marked kill on sight by all the other vampires in the city for the rest of his unlife. I'm sure the other players will be able to come up with some clever ways to kill him if legal Diablerie is on the table, and if not, you can use any of the various ideas in this thread for NPCs to send after him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:59:15-07:00","id":957004,"title":"","content":"It would be easy to kill them. But unless you plan on kicking them from your table they'll just make another character, and the rest of the coterie should be followed by the stigma of having been 'friends' with the psychopath.<br /> <br /> But providing they're not just acting out out of boredom or whatever you might just make aspects of the game more combat heavy so they have something to focus their character on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:10:50-07:00","id":957005,"title":"","content":"Agree with everyone else. Don't be afraid to get rid of him if it's best for the rest of the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T00:42:07-07:00","id":957451,"title":"","content":"Your very right I just, I've been in games with him before, but this is the first game I've hosted and he's started doing this. I don't want to kick him out and I just think if I kill his character I can finally establish to him this will happen if you keep making the same.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm to nice or to passiv but I don't want to start a fight with him out of character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T00:56:25-07:00","id":957453,"title":"","content":"Make him possessed by a spirit of murder: you can play him too to THANKS for this.<br /> Later, send him a pack composed of Storm Lord(Full Moon) and Hunter of Darkness (Irraka).<br /> Cheer.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:30:13-07:00","id":957467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957451#post957451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your very right I just, I've been in games with him before, but this is the first game I've hosted and he's started doing this. I don't want to kick him out and I just think if I kill his character I can finally establish to him this will happen if you keep making the same.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm to nice or to passiv but I don't want to start a fight with him out of character</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case and it's the first time he's acted in such fashion, it's probably a deliberate attempt to test your boundaries as a ST. Many players do stuff like this with impunity till STs get feed-up with the behavior and actual consequences happen. It's a good learning curve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:53:57-07:00","id":957472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957451#post957451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your very right I just, I've been in games with him before, but this is the first game I've hosted and he's started doing this. I don't want to kick him out and I just think if I kill his character I can finally establish to him this will happen if you keep making the same.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm to nice or to passiv but I don't want to start a fight with him out of character</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to go easy on him drop a hint before sending in the big guns. If he's got one of the highest unsanconed kill count in the city lots of people will want to take him out from Prince and Regents who don't want to clean up his mess to high Humanity neonates who think he's a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:37:26-07:00","id":957485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957472#post957472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to go easy on him drop a hint before sending in the big guns. If he's got one of the highest unsanconed kill count in the city lots of people will want to take him out from Prince and Regents who don't want to clean up his mess to high Humanity neonates who think he's a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's time to prepare the Lancea Et Sanctum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:44:38-07:00","id":957486,"title":"","content":"Maybe he can convince them his actions show a dedication to their course, he is scaring humans into being aware that they're not safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:47:27-07:00","id":957487,"title":"","content":"I think that to pay him back with his own coin would be satisfactory. I mean: he uses Obfuscate to run away? use Obfuscate to catch him with a surprise grapple/attack.<br /> Or with Auspex to see him trhough obfuscate.<br /> But I think also that showing him that there are more viable ways to surclass a kill-em-all character would be great too. Like with Dominate/Majesty without touching him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:23:17-07:00","id":957560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957451#post957451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your very right I just, I've been in games with him before, but this is the first game I've hosted and he's started doing this. I don't want to kick him out and I just think if I kill his character I can finally establish to him this will happen if you keep making the same.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm to nice or to passiv but I don't want to start a fight with him out of character</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be a fight. Just a talk between rational adults about the fact that his behavior is ruining the fun for other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:49:45-07:00","id":957619,"title":"","content":"Remember that people gathering around a table have, in general, a very simple and innocent goal - to have fun. Unless there is some complicated drama going behind the doors, he isn't doing this to sabotage your game or to spite you. Most probably, he finds this way to play fun, and he wants to have fun. I would be careful before doing anything to &quot;pay him with his own coin&quot; or anything like that, because in his perception, he is going to be suddenly punished for having fun and doing nothing wrong. That will only paint you as a bad guy in his eyes and birth negative emotions. I suggest talking, talking, talking, and talking. Don't be afraid to say &quot;It's too hard for me to GM this kind of character&quot;. It's ok to admit weakness or unability or not-wanting-to play in this way. Communicate your feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:57:41-07:00","id":957648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957619#post957619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that people gathering around a table have, in general, a very simple and innocent goal - to have fun. Unless there is some complicated drama going behind the doors, he isn't doing this to sabotage your game or to spite you. Most probably, he finds this way to play fun, and he wants to have fun. I would be careful before doing anything to &amp;quot;pay him with his own coin&amp;quot; or anything like that, because in his perception, he is going to be suddenly punished for having fun and doing nothing wrong. That will only paint you as a bad guy in his eyes and birth negative emotions. I suggest talking, talking, talking, and talking. Don't be afraid to say &amp;quot;It's too hard for me to GM this kind of character&amp;quot;. It's ok to admit weakness or unability or not-wanting-to play in this way. Communicate your feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait XD<br /> I said pay him with his own coin IN GAME. If you read my previous posts I said that I prefer to let a player do whatever he want and just pay the consequences. Because going around to kill vampires should have consequences in game. If he can handle it, in game, nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:17:58-07:00","id":957801,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of mages. You know there are mages who can summon sunlight? Directly! In an area! Many of these same mages are quite good at making magic items that can do the same thing. These items can even be used by normal mortals, not well, but still. But if you aren't using other super naturals in the game a bunch of mortals turned hunters (families of those killed) with Molotov cocktails will do just as well. As I remember it takes quite a bit of effort to heal damage from fire or sunlight. How many people has he killed? The families aren't pissed off? You don't have to kill him in one encounter. Hound him. Make him spend his blood. Damage him with fire. Let him kill more people so his humanity and sanity erode. Never forget the greatest asset mortals have . . . NUMBERS! Don't let up on him. Always have another hunter knocking on his door or throwing a flame at him. He'll kill most of them but two rise to replace every one he kills, and he leaves evidence of vampires to many times. Now the elders want him out of the city. If he want's to push his violence on the world make it clear that the world will push back. That's how I'd do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:22:31-07:00","id":957806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957648#post957648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait XD<br /> I said pay him with his own coin IN GAME. If you read my previous posts I said that I prefer to let a player do whatever he want and just pay the consequences. Because going around to kill vampires should have consequences in game. If he can handle it, in game, nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, this is clearly a problem that extends beyond in-game. If Chaos was comfortable just letting the character do whatever he wants and pay the in-character consequences, they would have just done that, or asked for advice about how best to do that. Since they asked for advice on how to deal with a player, and framed it in terms of the player's behavior disrupting the game, it's clear that the issue runs deeper than just needing a way to challenge the character.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is, if a player's actions are making the game less fun for you or the other players, answering that with in-character consequences is either going to encourage them to keep doing it (if they find those consequences fun), or it's going to make them feel like the ST is out to ruin their fun. If you just talk to them in person and say that what they're doing is making it hard for you to enjoy the game, most people will understand and adjust their behavior. The player probably just doesn't realize what they're doing is disruptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:08:38-07:00","id":957904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957806#post957806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, this is clearly a problem that extends beyond in-game. If Chaos was comfortable just letting the character do whatever he wants and pay the in-character consequences, they would have just done that, or asked for advice about how best to do that. Since they asked for advice on how to deal with a player, and framed it in terms of the player's behavior disrupting the game, it's clear that the issue runs deeper than just needing a way to challenge the character.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is, if a player's actions are making the game less fun for you or the other players, answering that with in-character consequences is either going to encourage them to keep doing it (if they find those consequences fun), or it's going to make them feel like the ST is out to ruin their fun. If you just talk to them in person and say that what they're doing is making it hard for you to enjoy the game, most people will understand and adjust their behavior. The player probably just doesn't realize what they're doing is disruptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you but my advice about in game consequences was aimed to let the player learn that if his character do this he is going to die. Obviously if the player will make always new character that do the same things, well yes, tell him your game doesn't fit with his way to play. But I think that at the third death he would quit by his own will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:19:08-07:00","id":957907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957904#post957904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you but my advice about in game consequences was aimed to let the player learn that if his character do this he is going to die. Obviously if the player will make always new character that do the same things, well yes, tell him your game doesn't fit with his way to play. But I think that at the third death he would quit by his own will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he would, maybe he wouldn't, but either way I bet he'd have appreciated just being <i>told</i> the ST didn't want him to run that sort of character, rather than being made to batter his head against a brick wall until he figures out why the ST keeps killing off his characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-25-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:33:11-07:00","id":957911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=957907#post957907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe he would, maybe he wouldn't, but either way I bet he'd have appreciated just being <i>told</i> the ST didn't want him to run that sort of character, rather than being made to batter his head against a brick wall until he figures out why the ST keeps killing off his characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree. Can't we just communicate? Use our words? We all tell our five year olds to do that, right, I'm not the only one who tells that to the kids?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T19:58:08-07:00","id":958574,"title":"","content":"If you want an unorthodox, super nice, (possible) solution how about this:<br /> He's now infamous to all the Kindred in the city. They all avoid him like the plague.<br /> But the Prince wants rid of his Sheriff. Maybe he's lost the respect of the vampires in the city. Maybe the Prince just hates him.<br /> <br /> The Prince gives the Nosferatu psycho the proverbial &quot;I'm going to make you an offer you can't refuse&quot; speech.<br /> Take the roll of Sheriff when the current holder &quot;vacates&quot; his position.<br /> The Prince only has one condition: all unsanctioned killing ends right now.<br /> <br /> The Prince makes it known, this is his only chance. His only choice:<br /> He agrees, and faces his toughest test in the current Sheriff.<br /> Or he refuses, and the Prince declares him Anathema, and his days are numbered.<br /> <br /> This would only work if your player is reasonable and can adapt. And elevating him wouldn't ruin the group power structure, or be seen as &quot;rewarding bad behaviour&quot; by him.<br /> <br /> The Prince essentially becomes the GM's proxy in this situation. You don't need to have the out of game talk with him. The leader of the city has it for you, and the player can't even pretend that he didn't know what was coming if he can't change his ways...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:45:25-07:00","id":958592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958574#post958574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want an unorthodox, super nice, (possible) solution how about this:<br /> He's now infamous to all the Kindred in the city. They all avoid him like the plague.<br /> But the Prince wants rid of his Sheriff. Maybe he's lost the respect of the vampires in the city. Maybe the Prince just hates him.<br /> <br /> The Prince gives the Nosferatu psycho the proverbial &amp;quot;I'm going to make you an offer you can't refuse&amp;quot; speech.<br /> Take the roll of Sheriff when the current holder &amp;quot;vacates&amp;quot; his position.<br /> The Prince only has one condition: all unsanctioned killing ends right now.<br /> <br /> The Prince makes it known, this is his only chance. His only choice:<br /> He agrees, and faces his toughest test in the current Sheriff.<br /> Or he refuses, and the Prince declares him Anathema, and his days are numbered.<br /> <br /> This would only work if your player is reasonable and can adapt. And elevating him wouldn't ruin the group power structure, or be seen as &amp;quot;rewarding bad behaviour&amp;quot; by him.<br /> <br /> The Prince essentially becomes the GM's proxy in this situation. You don't need to have the out of game talk with him. The leader of the city has it for you, and the player can't even pretend that he didn't know what was coming if he can't change his ways...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that this isn't a good in-character excuse for why the character would suddenly stop killing wantonly, but... What is up with this &quot;you don't need to have the out-of-character talk&quot; business, as if talking to your players is some kind of obligation to be avoided if possible? Are people like... Afraid to communicate with each other? Seriously, how hard is it to just be like &quot;Hey, dude, I was really hoping to run a more intrigue focused game, and your character killing dudes left and right is putting kind of a hink in that. Would you mind easing up on that, or making a less violent character instead?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T21:05:02-07:00","id":958595,"title":"","content":"Seriously. I feel like people thought I was joking when I commenting about telling the five year old to use her words, but no. I'm going to tell y'all what I would tell the five year old like six times a day--USE YOUR WORDS.<br /> <br /> Or write it down. Communicate, is the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T22:57:32-07:00","id":958615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958592#post958592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that this isn't a good in-character excuse for why the character would suddenly stop killing wantonly, but... What is up with this &quot;you don't need to have the out-of-character talk&quot; business...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with it. It's exactly what I would (and do) do.<br /> <br /> But OP has already been given that advice, and doesn't seem to want to use it, as he diesn't want to start a fight. So, I figured I might as well offer another way...<br /> <br /> Some people aren't good (or don't like) confronting people. And some people can't deal with being confronted. Maybe this &quot;problem player&quot; gives off is exactly that way.<br /> <br /> Seems like, as has been pointed out, the Player could be a problem player all round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","user":"FutureBondVillain","date":". 08-27-2016, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:06:06-07:00","id":958649,"title":"","content":"I talked with him, and after a long chat about how he wasn't in the wrong and that he was well within his rights to kill as he pleased he was removed, as I decided his attitude was unacceptable. Though I do feel like shit over having to do such a thing, but I suppose it had to be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:05:04-07:00","id":958675,"title":"","content":"Future advice - don't talk with people using judgemental statements of right and wrong. There is no &quot;right&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; way to play the game. There is only &quot;fun for me&quot;, &quot;fun for you&quot;, &quot;fun for us&quot;, &quot;unfun for me&quot;, &quot;unfun for you&quot;, &quot;unfun for us&quot; and combinations of these. Using statements like &quot;you are playing wrong&quot; is a sure-fire way to aggravate the argument and make another person feel personally attacked - in many cases, this will blind them to your actual arguments and trigger buttons in their brain that force them to defend themselves (and often, best defence is to attack you). &quot;I don't enjoy GMing these kinds of situations, I'm sorry I can't handle it, is there anything else you would like to play?&quot; has much bigger chance of making negotiations, well, negotiations, than &quot;You are ruining the game and playing wrong, stop or else&quot;. <br /> People don't like a) being told that they are doing something wrong, and b) feeling blamed for ruining something. It might hurt your pride, but in future, I would suggest with sharing the blame; &quot;I'm sorry I'm not good enough to GM this kind of character, could we try figuring something else that will be fun for you?&quot; and so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:06:57-07:00","id":958709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958649#post958649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I talked with him, and after a long chat about how he wasn't in the wrong and that he was well within his rights to kill as he pleased he was removed, as I decided his attitude was unacceptable. Though I do feel like shit over having to do such a thing, but I suppose it had to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sucks, man. It's always sad to have to tell a player they're not a good fit for your game, especially a friend. But in the long run it's better than creating a passive-aggressive player vs. GM environment in game. Here's hoping things improve for you and your group from here on out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:17:35-07:00","id":958714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958649#post958649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I talked with him, and after a long chat about how he wasn't in the wrong and that he was well within his rights to kill as he pleased he was removed, as I decided his attitude was unacceptable. Though I do feel like shit over having to do such a thing, but I suppose it had to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to hear. We're kind of trained to think we have to be able to work with everyone, but that's unrealistic, and the most important thing is to keep the space safe and welcoming for the majority of your group. It sounds like that's what you did, and I'm proud of you for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:35:57-07:00","id":958717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958649#post958649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I talked with him, and after a long chat about how he wasn't in the wrong and that he was well within his rights to kill as he pleased he was removed, as I decided his attitude was unacceptable. Though I do feel like shit over having to do such a thing, but I suppose it had to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be, the guy made a twink pc and from here it looks like they just wanted to cause chaos. It's disrespectful to you as a story teller and to the other players. The fact that they can't admit they are in the wrong speaks more about themselves then a anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 08-27-2016, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:38:21-07:00","id":958735,"title":"","content":"There is no reason for you to think that dude &quot;made a twink pc&quot; and that they just wanted to cause chaos. Just because they can't defend themselves here doesn't mean it's ok to badmouth them. Again, in majority of cases, people just want to have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:15:24-07:00","id":958745,"title":"","content":"Other than the fact that the OP said this &quot;Your very right I just, I've been in games with him before, but this is the first game I've hosted and he's started doing this.&quot; <br /> <br /> Clearly the player was being a disruptive jerk with the intention of seeing if he could walk all over the storyteller. If he was just experimenting with a character type he normally doesn't play, he should have taken the numerous hints in-game to knock it off instead of pushing it to the point where it necessitated an out-of-character warning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-27-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:21:54-07:00","id":958765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958735#post958735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no reason for you to think that dude &amp;quot;made a twink pc&amp;quot; and that they just wanted to cause chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see, strength 5, double bite damage thing, full grapple style, some potency, and riding the wave. Sounds kinda twink-ish. <br /> <br /> Wouldn't get the hint that they are causing problems both in and out of game? Then had the gaul to tell the story teller they have all rights to do what they have been doing....let's be an adult about this, clearly this person wasn't....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:38:07-07:00","id":958772,"title":"","content":"Some people want to play everything like it's D&amp;D. I wouldn't let anyone like that anywhere near one of my games. Because I'm really not interested in those type of games.<br /> <br /> I'm not one to say &quot;you're doing it wrong&quot; if you're playing Vampire like that... Except, who am I kidding, that's exactly what I'd say.<br /> <br /> The character concept could even work if done in cooperation with the group, and Storyteller - a psycho who gets all this power and thinks he owns the world, until he learns there's always bigger sharks out there. Adapt or die.<br /> <br /> That was obviously not the intention here though. Good riddance to the player. Don't feel a seconds guilt over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:49:05-07:00","id":958799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958765#post958765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't get the hint that they are causing problems both in and out of game? Then had the gaul to tell the story teller they have all rights to do what they have been doing....let's be an adult about this, clearly this person wasn't....</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing devil's advocate here: It's true - the player has all the the right in the world to portray his character however the hell he wanted. It's then up to the ST to enforce consequences for his actions if he couldn't take the hint.<br /> <br /> I've seen that plenty of times: New ST, let's see what we can get away with doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:13:39-07:00","id":958811,"title":"","content":"I kinda agree, but only up to a point Malus.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to have in game responses play out. It shows him, and the group, the way the world works, and how there's repercussions for their actions.<br /> <br /> However imagine: at the end of this &quot;arc&quot; the character is killed. The player then creates another psycho nutjob. Ad infinitum.<br /> <br /> In game repercussions can't deal with that. You have a player that is just happy to destroy the game, over and over.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller ideally it is very easy to say to the player &quot;your character is going off the reservation here, I'm giving you this one and only warning that I'm not going to protect him. The world will respond how it responds.&quot;<br /> <br /> But equally the player should probably also be saying &quot;I understand what my character is doing here is extreme. If it's ok with you I'd like to play it out, and see what happens. I understand if he ends up dead because of what he's done.&quot;<br /> <br /> So sadly, no, I don't think you can rely solely on either an in or out of game approach. Really you need to use both hammers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:50:19-07:00","id":958822,"title":"","content":"I really don't understand why everyone here seems so sure that this specific player is going to make a crazy killer &quot;ad infinitum&quot;, everytime he going to die in consequences of his &quot;in game&quot; actions. Why couldn't him understand that his actions, like in the real world, have consequences and why don't give him the opportunity to grow up with his way to play according to these experiences. <br /> Probably he wouldn't change and send him away gonna be the only way to handle him, but why take it for garanted. Sorry but I don't agree with this way to act.<br /> <br /> At the second or third failed attempt, then could be right to do as you say in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-27-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:09:19-07:00","id":958830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958799#post958799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing devil's advocate here: It's true - the player has all the the right in the world to portray his character however the hell he wanted. It's then up to the ST to enforce consequences for his actions if he couldn't take the hint.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only a viable option if the ST is comfortable running a game where a significant portion of the story is dedicated to the consequences of one character's murderous actions. Not everyone wants to run that kind of game. Ideally, there shouldn't be a need to &quot;take the hint&quot;, because you shouldn't be hinting. You should be talking to your players clearly an directly so that everyone is on the same page about what kind of game they're playing. That way you don't get one guy with the wrong idea, thinking it's a high-simulation sandbox where anything goes and you deal with the natural consequences, when the ST was trying to run a high-narrative procedural crime drama, where the players all work together to solve a mystery. You just all know, from the beginning, what kind of game you're playing and what the expectations are, and can decide to participate or not participate as suits their interests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958822#post958822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand why everyone here seems so sure that this specific player is going to make a crazy killer &quot;ad infinitum&quot;, everytime he going to die in consequences of his &quot;in game&quot; actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumptions based on not talking to the player. Ideally, there should be no need to assume that the player is maliciously trying to test the ST's boundaries, or disrupt the game. Nor that they are insistent on playing a game of murderhobos, nor any other assumed motivation, because you can just <i>ask them</i> and then there's no need to assume. You just know why they're doing it, because you're communicating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-27-2016, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:43:23-07:00","id":958845,"title":"","content":"I never said you shouldn't talk with him. I just saying that I would starting with in game consequences: you kill a vamp diplomat; as far as I know killing a kindred is a serious offense, and being hunted by the sheriff should not be unexpected. He kills the sheriff? Blood hunting and final death. <br /> At this point the ST can/must gives polite explaination as you said. <br /> If the next PC stills in his crazy killing way well, now I would consider to remove the player. <br /> Finally there isn't nothing wrong in playing a monster in a game baser on monster. It should just been played in a smart way. You just can't kill anything you want to kill.<br /> Anyway it's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:15:17-07:00","id":958864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958845#post958845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said you shouldn't talk with him. I just saying that I would starting with in game consequences: you kill a vamp diplomat; as far as I know killing a kindred is a serious offense, and being hunted by the sheriff should not be unexpected. He kills the sheriff? Blood hunting and final death. <br /> At this point the ST can/must gives polite explaination as you said. <br /> If the next PC stills in his crazy killing way well, now I would consider to remove the player. <br /> Finally there isn't nothing wrong in playing a monster in a game baser on monster. It should just been played in a smart way. You just can't kill anything you want to kill.<br /> Anyway it's just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think we're on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:49:02-07:00","id":958895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/956214-looking-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-a-player?p=958845#post958845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said you shouldn't talk with him. I just saying that I would starting with in game consequences: you kill a vamp diplomat; as far as I know killing a kindred is a serious offense, and being hunted by the sheriff should not be unexpected. He kills the sheriff? Blood hunting and final death.<br /> At this point the ST can/must gives polite explanation as you said.<br /> If the next PC stills in his crazy killing way well, now I would consider to remove the player.<br /> Finally there isn't nothing wrong in playing a monster in a game baser on monster. It should just been played in a smart way. You just can't kill anything you want to kill.<br /> Anyway it's just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's my MO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}